    "placementHash": "sha256:19f7f0c7750aa83756971593611a56da63e7eee45b3abfacd2ed5ba0bb1411c6",
    "notes": "PMTiles locates the station wings and rail yard. The long Karasuma edge defines the signed heading. Terrain and paving masks seat the entrance and rail floors. Six sampled doorways and eleven rail lanes clear the authored geometry. The podium, outer building wings, rail centerlines and platform shelter footprints follow PMTiles. Photo interpretation supplies the atrium section, public circulation and individual facade bays. The forecourt elevations follow open Terrarium approach samples. The station floors and railway deck elevations are reconstructed to bridge high samples over the built site. The model represents the exterior, the public atrium and the above-ground track concourses. Stairs, escalators and railway fixtures are static geometry."
  },
